**Move mock implementations to `beforeEach` blocks and stabilize git-dependent test.**

The current mock setup has inline mock implementations inside individual test cases (lines 125–137), which violates Vitest patterns. Additionally, the first test relies on real git history and will fail on shallow clones. Move all mock behavior to `beforeEach`, use `vi.mocked()` to access the mock, and mock the git output for all cases. The async factory pattern is valid as-is; do not add `{ spy: true }` as that option is an alternative to the factory, not compatible with it.

<details>
<summary>Refactor mock setup</summary>

```diff
 import { describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';
+import { beforeEach } from 'vitest';

 import { executeCommandSync } from 'storybook/internal/common';

 import { getProjectSince, normalizeGitUrl, unhashedProjectId } from './anonymous-id';

 vi.mock('storybook/internal/common', async (importOriginal) => {
-  const actual = await importOriginal();
+  const actual = await importOriginal<typeof import('storybook/internal/common')>();

   return {
     ...actual,
     executeCommandSync: vi.fn(actual.executeCommandSync),
   };
 });
+
+const mockedExecuteCommandSync = vi.mocked(executeCommandSync);
+
+beforeEach(() => {
+  mockedExecuteCommandSync.mockReset();
+  mockedExecuteCommandSync.mockReturnValue('2015-12-11T10:54:01.000Z');
+});

 describe('getProjectSince', () => {
   it('returns the Storybook creation date from git log output', () => {
     expect(getProjectSince()).toEqual(new Date('2015-12-11T10:54:01.000Z'));
   });

   it('returns undefined if git log output is empty', () => {
-    vi.mocked(executeCommandSync).mockReturnValue('');
+    mockedExecuteCommandSync.mockReturnValue('');

     expect(getProjectSince()).toBeUndefined();
   });

   it('returns undefined if git log fails', () => {
-    vi.mocked(executeCommandSync).mockImplementation(() => {
+    mockedExecuteCommandSync.mockImplementation(() => {
       throw new Error('git not available');
     });
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@code/core/src/telemetry/anonymous-id.test.ts` around lines 1 - 14, The tests
currently set per-test inline mocks and rely on real git output; move the
executeCommandSync mock setup into a beforeEach block and use
vi.mocked(executeCommandSync) to set return values there so all tests get
controlled, deterministic git output (mock the git command responses used by
getProjectSince/normalizeGitUrl/unhashedProjectId); remove per-test mock
implementations (lines 125–137) and instead in beforeEach call
vi.mocked(executeCommandSync).mockImplementation(...) or .mockReturnValue(...)
to stabilize the git-dependent test — keep the async factory vi.mock(...) as-is
and do not add the { spy: true } option.
```

</details>

